    <briefdescription>
<para>Full 6-DOF pose for a single hand joint. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Extends <computeroutput><ref refid="structILLIXR_1_1data__format_1_1pose_1_1pose__base" kindref="compound">pose_base</ref></computeroutput> with per-joint <computeroutput>joint_location_flags</computeroutput>, a linear velocity, and a joint-sphere radius.</para>
<para><computeroutput>pose_base::valid</computeroutput> is set to <computeroutput>true</computeroutput> when both ORIENTATION_VALID and POSITION_VALID are set in <computeroutput>location_flags</computeroutput>, providing a single &quot;is this usable?&quot; check for consumers that do not need the finer-grained distinction. Consumers that do need it (e.g. physics that should only apply velocity when POSITION_TRACKED is set) should read <computeroutput>location_flags</computeroutput> directly. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
